/* book: the chapter, paragraph by paragraph (first sentences):
   - A gun forms a beam of current I₀ accelerated through V₀, so electrons enter at v₀ = √(2eV₀/m) = 0.593 × 10⁶ √V₀ m/s.
   - Take as reference the electron that crosses when the gap voltage is zero and rising.
   - βi = sin(θg/2)/(θg/2) is the beam coupling coefficient of a gap of transit angle θg = ωd/v₀ (d = gap width); θ₀ is the drift transit angle over the drift length L; X is the bunching parameter.
   - The fundamental RF current of the bunched beam is 2I₀J₁(X), largest at X = 1.841, where J₁ = 0.582.
   - A reflex klystron is an oscillator.
   - T′ is the round-trip time, N the mode number (¾, 1¾, 2¾ …), VR the repeller voltage magnitude and L the repeller distance.
   - Each mode has its own repeller voltage, and only modes with VR > 0 exist.
   - A cylindrical magnetron has a cathode of radius a inside an anode of radius b cut into N cavities.
   - B₀c in tesla, V₀c in volts, a and b in metres; fc is the cyclotron frequency with B₀ in tesla.
   - Above cutoff the electrons form a rotating space-charge wheel whose spokes keep step with the RF field across the cavity gaps.
*/
