/* book Worked example: Q: A two-cavity klystron has V₀ = 1200 V, I₀ = 30 mA, f = 4 GHz, gap width d = 1 mm and drift length L = 3 cm. Find v₀, the gap coupling coefficient, the drift transit angle, the input gap voltage V₁ for maximum bunching, and the maximum efficiency.
   1. v₀ = 0.593 × 10⁶ × √1200 = 2.054 × 10⁷ m/s (0.068c, so non-relativistic).
   2. ω = 2π × 4 × 10⁹ = 2.513 × 10¹⁰ rad/s. Gap angle θg = ωd/v₀ = 2.513 × 10¹⁰ × 10⁻³/2.054 × 10⁷ = 1.223 rad.
   3. βi = sin(0.6117)/0.6117 = 0.5742/0.6117 = 0.939.
   4. Drift angle θ₀ = ωL/v₀ = 2.513 × 10¹⁰ × 0.03/2.054 × 10⁷ = 36.70 rad (5.84 cycles).
   5. Maximum bunching at X = 1.841: V₁ = 2V₀X/(βiθ₀) = 2 × 1200 × 1.841/(0.939 × 36.70) = 128.2 V.
   6. Beam RF current 2I₀J₁(1.841) = 2 × 30 × 0.582 = 34.9 mA; maximum efficiency 58.2 % of V₀I₀ = 36 W, so at most about 21 W of RF.
   Answer: v₀ = 2.05 × 10⁷ m/s, βi = 0.939, θ₀ = 36.7 rad, V₁ = 128.2 V for X = 1.841, and at most 58.2 % (about 21 W of the 36 W input). */
